  "step_3": "The decision reason prioritizes the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome, treating outcome differences as negligible. In this case, the favorable outcome is interpreted as 0€ (no loss), which occurs with 50% probability in A and 0% in B. The individual explicitly highlights this 50% chance of no loss in A and contrasts it with the certainty of loss in B, which aligns directly with the core logic of the decision reason. Although the individual mentions their financial situation, the decisive justification is the presence of a 'high' chance to avoid loss in A. This matches both the information considered (probability of favorable outcome) and the rule of the decision reason (prefer higher probability of favorable outcome). The verbal emphasis on the 50% chance of zero loss as a key advantage strongly indicates use of this reason, even if not stated formally. The outcome difference (-500 vs. -1000) is effectively treated as secondary, consistent with the reason's assumption of negligible outcome differences.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
