  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes preferring the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome, treating outcome differences as negligible. The favorable outcome is reasonably interpreted as 0 Euros. Lottery A offers 75% chance, B offers 50%, so the reason favors A. The individual considers the probability of 'loss' and notes that A has half the loss probability of B (25% vs 50%), leading to a preference for A. The individual’s focus on the likelihood of avoiding loss (i.e., achieving 0 Euros) and lack of discussion on loss magnitudes aligns with treating outcome differences as negligible and prioritizing the chance of the best outcome. Therefore, both the relevant information (probability of favorable outcome) and the justification (lower chance of loss) match the decision reason. The reasoning process described is consistent with the rule specified by the decision reason.",
